see it's very easy
if you have normal

252
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:28,930
proprioception to know
even the slightest

253
00:10:28,930 --> 00:10:31,500
movement to be able to
tell. But a lot of times,

254
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,960
people with peripheral
neuropathies and

255
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,840
other vascular diseases
in their distal

256
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,780
extremities oftentimes
have a very difficult

257
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,920
time determining
proprioception. So it's got

258
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:41,420
to be done subtly.
It's got to be done

259
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,940
very, very, very
carefully to pay attention

260
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:47,460
to which side is or
is not being affected.

261
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,980
Now, discriminative
sensations.

262
00:10:51,410 --> 00:10:53,040
This tests the
ability of the

263
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,640
sensory cortex
to correlate,

264
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,400
analyze, or
interpret sensations.

265
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,860
Touch and position
sense need to be intact

266
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:01,740
for tests. All right.
Absence or decrease in

267
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:04,920
discriminative sensation
includes a lesion,

268
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,100
possibly most likely
in the sensory cortex.

269
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:09,000
And once again,
patient's eyes should be

270
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,480
closed for all of
these discriminative

271
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:13,170
tests. We need to have
touch and position

272
00:11:13,170 --> 00:11:15,140
sense intact. Otherwise,
they won't be able

273
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:16,740
to perform these
tests accurately and

274
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:18,380
you won't be able to
get accurate results.

275
00:11:19,930 --> 00:11:22,030
What are some of the
discriminative tests?

276
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,720
OK, these are tests.

277
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,220
There are three most
commonly that we

278
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:28,260
use here. Stereognosis
is the identifying

279
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:30,600
of an object in
touch. So you take a

280
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,660
very common option,
be a pen or a pen

281
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:35,320
cap or a key, as in
this picture here.

282
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,280
You have the patient
close their eyes,

283
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,700
place the object
in their hand,

284
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:40,280
and simply ask them
if they can feel

285
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,240
it and what they
think the object is.

286
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:45,020
And then usually
most of you will be

287
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:47,560
able to determine
that. But again, people

288
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,280
who have lacked
position sense and

289
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,700
things like that
can have an often

290
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,640
difficult time telling
what the object is.

291
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:55,760
Second, grapesthesia
is number

292
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,500
identification, where
you can identify

293
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,380
the number drawn on
a patient's palm.

294
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,820
In the picture, we
use a pen so that it

295
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:04,220
illustrates what you're
doing. You can simply

296
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:07,640
use a cotton tip
applicator or a sharp

297
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:10,420
end of a pen cap that's
not on and just draw

298
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:12,340
the number without
drawing. We don't

299
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:14,200
want people drawing
all over people's hands

300
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,600
in labs, so you don't
need to specifically

301
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:18,280
draw the number, but
just for illustrative

302
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,240
purposes, that's what
we're doing here.

303
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,760
And then next is two
-point discrimination.

304
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:26,200
Taking a paperclip and
touching two places

305
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:28,700
simultaneously using
the open ends will help

306
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:31,760
determine if the patient
can feel one or both

307
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:33,940
points. Normal
minimal distance for

308
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:35,960
discrimination here will
vary for different parts

309
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,280
of the body. You know,
when there's more

310
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:40,000
nerve endings, you can
often tell a very, very

311
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,360
close distance between
the paperclips. So,

312
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:45,760
but people with significant
diminished sensation

313
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,880
and discrimination
will have a very hard

314
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,700
time determining those
points. So you start

315
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:53,100
as close as you can.
If they can't tell,

316
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:55,740
they move it a millimeter
or two further apart

317
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:59,120
and ask the patient
if they feel one, two,

318
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:01,560
or ask them what they
feel. And if they say

319
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,240
they feel it, ask them
how many points they

320
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,820
feel. And normal,
obviously, is two points.

321
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,980
Here's some more
discriminative sensation

322
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:13,420
testing. This one's
point localization.

323
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:16,460
Again, it's intuitive
and simplistic

324
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:19,040
in its way. It's
performed with

325
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:20,760
the patient's eyes
closed. You briefly

326
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:22,660
touch any place
on their skin.

327
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:25,960
Upper body, lower
body, arms, whatever,

328
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,340
you know, you want
to test on something

329
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,420
that's easily
accessible and then

330
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:31,800
ask the patient
to open their eyes

331
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,600
and point to the
place that's touched.

332
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,380
So you briefly
touch it, you remove

333
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:37,490
the object and ask
him to literally

334
00:13:37,490 --> 00:13:39,580
demonstrate where
you had just touched.

335
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:41,380
And if there's a
patient with a lesion in

336
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:43,620
the sensory cortex,
their ability to localize

337
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:45,840
that point will be
significantly impaired.

338
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:49,540
And then next is
extinction. So, again, with

339
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:51,960
the patient's eyes
closed, we simultaneously

340
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,700
stimulate areas on
both sides of the

341
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:56,320
body, generally the
same point, such as the

342
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,740
biceps or the upper
arms in this picture.

343
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,160
The patient will identify

344
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,860
the location of
the stimulus.

345
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:05,100
With the sensory cortex
lesions, only one

346
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:07,080
stimulus may be felt,
and this stimulus

347
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:09,240
that is not recognized
is extinguished.

348
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,720
And it would be on
the contralateral

349
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,160
side that is being
affected. So it's

350
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:14,540
one way you can
tell if there's an

351
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,300
impairment of the
sensory cortex due

352
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:19,160
to the contralateral
sensory loss.

353
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:24,260
Here are some
techniques that

354
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:25,700
we often include
towards the

355
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:28,560
end of the
neurologic lecture.

356
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:30,060
We'll go through each one

357
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:31,340
of these individually.

358
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:34,300
Brudinsky and Koenig
signs are both tests

359
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:36,860
for meningitis. Then
we have some tests

360
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:39,960
for cervical
radiculopathy or herniated

361
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,620
discs in the neck,
including axial compression

362
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:45,660
and pyramidal
distraction, as well as

363
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:47,280
the Spurling test, by
the way. It's skipped

364
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,320
down a spot. And
then we'll go into a

365
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:51,460
few other tests with
using the legs and

366
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:54,100
looking for lumbar
radiculopathy and possibly

367
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:56,300
a malignering patient
in the UBER test.

368
00:14:57,720 --> 00:15:01,200
All right, meningeal
signs, important. This

369
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:04,780
is a condition that
you definitely want

370
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:08,100
to identify early,
since untreated, this

371
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,160
can cause significant
morbidity mortality.

372
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:12,920
Meningitis is an
extremely important

373
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:15,600
diagnosis to make
early on, especially

374
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,500
if there's signs
of fever, neck

375
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,520
stiffness, and mental
status changes.

376
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:21,940
This test is suspected
when meningeal

377
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,820
inflammation from
either meningitis or

378
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:26,160
subarachnoid hemorrhage
can be present, and the

379
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:27,860
two most common
tests that we will be

380
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,120
practicing in lab are
Brudzinski and Kernan.

381
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,580
What do these signs do?

382
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:34,680
Brudzinski.

383
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:37,720
When you lie the
patient supine and you

384
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:41,240
slightly flex the
head and neck forward,

385
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:45,880
as you have this
patient licepine flat,

386
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:48,470
and when you lift the
head and neck forward,

387
00:15:48,470 --> 00:15:51,220
flexion, there would
be, if the Brudzinski

388
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:53,490
sign is present,
there'd be a natural

389
00:15:53,490 --> 00:15:56,360
response for the hip and
knee, or I should say

390
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:58,120
pathological response
for the hip and knee,

391
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:02,280
relax will now be
flexed automatically as

392
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:05,440
you flex the neck.
There'll be a simultaneous

393
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,540
flexion of both
hips and knees. Very

394
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:11,320
important to recognize
this. Due to a

395
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:13,300
constant inflammation
along throughout the

396
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:16,760
entire spinal cord,
any sort of problem or

397
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:19,320
irritation of the
cervical spine will cause

398
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:23,080
a subsequent
inflammation or response

399
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,820
to the lower extremity.
And that's why we

400
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:27,140
get this response.
The second test is

401
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:30,740
Kerning's. This is done
on the leg this time,

402
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,820
where you have the
patient's leg flex at

403
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:34,740
the hip and knee while
the patient's lying

404
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:38,040
supine. The physician
takes the leg and

405
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,580
flexes it as it is
shown in this picture.

406
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:44,460
Once the leg is flexed
at the knee and the

407
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:47,160
ankle, you slowly extend
the leg and straighten

408
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,360
the knee. A positive
Kerning's sign would

409
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,260
be pain and increase
resistance to knee

410
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:54,640
extension as you bring
the leg back down. How

411
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:57,000
can we remember what
these tests are? Very

412
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,160
easy. I like to remember
B for Brutzynski is

413
00:17:00,160 --> 00:17:02,500
brain, therefore it's
the neck, and K for

414
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:05,700
Koenig is the knee.
So K Koenig is done at

415
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:08,180
the lower extremity, B
Brutzynski is done at

416
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:09,840
the upper extremity.
And once again, we'll

417
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:14,480
be practicing these
important tests in lab.

418
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:19,140
Axial compression test.
This is a test for

419
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:21,820
cervical neck impingement.
With the patient

420
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:24,140
seated just as such
in the picture and

421
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:27,020
the physician standing
behind, you rest

422
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:29,540
the elbows on the
shoulders and gently place

423
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:31,860
a downward compression
with your hands

424
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:34,340
resting on top of the
patient's head. You

425
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:38,480
exert a downward
force firmly, but not

426
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,820
causing an increased
amount of pain, all

427
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,000
right? The test is positive
if pain or neurologic

428
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
symptoms are reproduced
in the cervical

429
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,320
spine and or upper
extremity. As soon

430
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,400
as the patient reports
any discomfort, the

431
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,560
test should be
completed, and it should

432
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:54,360
be deemed a positive
test, okay? So this

433
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:57,080
is how the axial
compression test is done.

434
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,800
Straightforward, the
patient is looking

435
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,880
ahead. There's no side
bending or rotation,

436
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,340
and it's a simple
straight downward force.

437
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:07,500
Framal distraction,
okay? This is a test

438
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,640
for cervical nerve
impingement. So with

439
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,420
the patient seated
on the table, the

440
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:13,640
examiner places one
hand under the patient's

441
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,680
shin as seen here,
with the other hand

442
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,620
under the occiput,
the back of the head.

443
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,720
Gently, an upward
traction force

444
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,360
applied on the
cervical spine.

445
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:23,500
Now, normally, if the
patient is experiencing

446
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,420
symptoms of cervical
impingement,

447
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:27,900
which could be pain
at the neck, shooting

448
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:29,820
pain down the arms
or the shoulders,

449
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,560
oftentimes a positive
test here is a

450
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:35,560
reduction of pain due
to the traction force.

451
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,760
It would actually
make the patient feel

452
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,280
better. So once again,
the test is positive.

453
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:41,260
The pain or
neurologic symptoms of

454
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:43,220
the cervical spine
and or upper extremity

455
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,660
are reduced with the
traction force. In

456
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:46,780
other words, it's
almost like a treatment

457
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,720
technique that we
help to relieve the

458
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,840
pressure on the spine,
and a positive test

459
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,780
would actually be a
reduction in pain.

460
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:56,660
Squirling test, something
also very commonly

461
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:59,540
done. It's been
around for years, all

462
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,560
right, but it's an
important test to recognize.

463
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:03,780
This is a test for
cervical nerve root

464
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:06,320
compression. It's
simple. It's similar to

465
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:08,400
the axial pyramidal
compression test with a

466
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:12,020
slight rotatory component.
So as you can see

467
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,780
with the physician
standing behind the

468
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:15,920
patient, having the
patient look over their

469
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,880
shoulder and then up at
the ceiling. So you're

470
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:20,380
applying sort of
like an extension and

471
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:23,700
a rotation, rotatory
force. That's when the

472
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:26,020
downward compression
as seen by the red

473
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:28,440
arrow pointing down is
applied to the patient's

474
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:32,280
head. Okay. Very,
very important. And we

475
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,600
were going to review
this in lab, and the

476
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:35,020
scholars are going to
be reviewing this as

477
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:37,320
well. The maneuver
reproduces the neck pain

478
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:39,340
with radiation to the
arm on the same side

479
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,460
that the head is
turned to. If there is

480
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:44,080
pain simply with the
positioning in the head

481
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:48,580
or just moving it into
rotation or extension,

482
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,780
it is not necessary
to apply downward

483
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:52,920
pressure. It's considered
a positive test.

484
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:54,860
Ultimately, we're
trying to protect the

485
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,900
sanctity and well-being
of the patient. And a

486
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,080
positive test, just by
putting it in a position,

487
00:20:00,080 --> 00:20:02,180
it's not going to
create any less pain.

488
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,720
It's going to create
more discomfort. So we

489
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:05,780
would consider that
a positive test. So

490
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:07,700
slightly different than
the axial pyramidal

491
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:11,380
compression is the
Spurling with the extension

492
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:14,100
and rotatory component,
which really isolates

493
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:16,120
the side of the nerve
root compression.

494
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,820
Next, we have the
straight leg raise with

495
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:22,400
Braggart's test. This
is a test for radicular

496
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:24,520
sciatic nerve pain.
As you can see, the

497
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,380
patient is lying
supine with their legs

498
